1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,227
The ladder progresses through apprentice,
builder, deployment owner, multiplier, and system

2
00:00:05,297 --> 00:00:09,649
designer. Its exit tests concern
observable work in context.

3
00:00:09,719 --> 00:00:13,601
Course completion does not
automatically satisfy those tests.

4
00:00:13,671 --> 00:00:18,429
Use the daily, weekly, monthly, and
quarterly cadence as a development aid.

5
00:00:18,499 --> 00:00:23,128
Select a manageable practice commitment,
collect evidence, and seek feedback.

6
00:00:23,198 --> 00:00:29,193
Real workplace practice should respect data
access, customer confidentiality, operating

7
00:00:29,263 --> 00:00:31,695
authority, and applicable procedures.

8
00:00:31,765 --> 00:00:35,925
A learner finishes the prototype and
calls themselves a deployment owner.

9
00:00:35,995 --> 00:00:40,731
They have not worked with real users or
performed an outcome reading after production

10
00:00:40,801 --> 00:00:46,987
adoption. Their portfolio demonstrates simulated
practice, with field evidence still pending.

11
00:00:47,057 --> 00:00:51,836
Pause the video and complete this exercise
before opening the worked response.

12
00:00:51,906 --> 00:00:58,071
Write a 30-day practice plan with one user
observation, one prediction, and one review of

13
00:00:58,141 --> 00:00:59,187
evidence.

14
00:00:59,257 --> 00:01:03,353
Week one: observe a permitted
workflow and map the actual decision.

15
00:01:03,423 --> 00:01:06,388
Week two: co-author a
small frame with its owner.

16
00:01:06,458 --> 00:01:10,959
Week three: run an authorized bounded
experiment with a written prediction.

17
00:01:11,029 --> 00:01:14,997
Week four: compare results and
identify one reusable lesson.

18
00:01:15,067 --> 00:01:20,678
If workplace access is unavailable, use a
second simulation and label it accordingly.

19
00:01:20,748 --> 00:01:24,332
Does course completion establish
the deployment- owner stage?

20
00:01:24,402 --> 00:01:27,367
A. No, the stage requires field evidence B.

21
00:01:27,437 --> 00:01:29,528
Yes, after watching videos C.

22
00:01:29,598 --> 00:01:31,667
Yes, if the self-rating is high.

23
00:01:31,737 --> 00:01:33,188
The best answer is A.

24
00:01:33,258 --> 00:01:37,759
Keep educational achievement separate
from verified career capability.
